WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.530
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and my Game of
Thrones Season 4 countdown continues.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:30.060
We’re within 30 days of the premiere and
they just posted a brand new trailer with

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.370
a bunch of new footage with a really tall
surprise that gives us an idea for just how

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.200
quickly the plot is going to be moving relative
to the books.

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.820
If you’re finding me for the first time
I’m doing a month long video countdown to

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:42.180
the season 4 premiere.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.460
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:47.300
I’m even doing a weekly giveaway for each
new episode once the season starts.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:51.180
So just like my previous breakdowns this is
going to be a shot for shot analysis of the

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.180
new footage.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.190
I’m going to exclude anything that was in
a previous trailer.

00:00:55.190 --> 00:00:58.450
Careful for spoilers in case you don’t want
to know anything about season 4.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:00:59.660
Here we go!

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:04.030
Starting off with a nice closeup shot of Widow’s
Wail, Joffrey’s new sword made from smelting

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:06.550
Ned Stark’s valyrian Blade.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.580
Then there’s a new shot of Sansa enduring
more of Joffrey weapon play time.

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:14.250
Which cuts to her recounting the Red Wedding
with new husband Tyrion.

00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:17.500
She’s got a lot to cry about this season.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:21.479
Next is a scene of Ramsay Snow joining his
father Roose Bolton.

00:01:21.479 --> 00:01:26.040
As mad as Roose seemed for aiding in the Red
Wedding, he’s still not as crazy as Ramsay.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:32.160
I always thought of the two of them like an
evil version of Ned Stark and Jon Snow.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:36.380
More Sansa sleeping in a room that looks like
a cell and might as well be.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:40.000
At least Tyrion isn’t making her sleep in
his bed.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.280
Then we finally get another nice long scene
with Oberyn Martell talking to Cersei about

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:47.369
the value of revenge.

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:51.280
For people who haven’t read the books, this
scene is incredibly ironic.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:54.030
Hopefully during the season they’ll explain
why that is.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.580
They’re both looking for revenge.

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.830
Here’s another slightly better look at the
city gates of Mereen.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:04.550
Then Barristan Selmy counseling Daenerys and
it flows nicely into a nice speech of hers

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:07.270
about bringing Justice to the city.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:12.160
The shots of the unsullied army are all repeated
from previous trailers, but the next shot,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:15.260
this guy is brand new and somewhat spoilery.

00:02:15.260 --> 00:02:20.770
It’s the Titan of Braavos, the place where
Arya’s Dancing Master Syrio Forel and Jaquen

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.440
H’ghar are from.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.010
Remember Arya’s coin, it’s a Braavosi
coin.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:30.569
I’ll let you rewatch the episode if you
don’t remember his instructions on how to

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:33.090
use the coin and what it does.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.570
Then there’s another shot of Daenerys' Unsullied
traveling.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:39.520
They’re trying to give us a visual reminder
of just how big her army is.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.300
I love the synchronicity of their movements
too.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.900
Grey Worm is actually the one that commands
them, Daenerys gives orders to him and he

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.110
gives them to the Unsullied.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:51.050
Then there’s my second favorite shot.

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:52.550
All three dragons.

00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:56.760
Look at how much bigger Drogon is than Rhaegal
and Viserion.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:58.840
They can hunt on their own now, especially
Drogon.

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.000
And it becomes a huge problem as they get
bigger.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.910
It’s like trying to raise a wild animal
like a Tiger in your home.

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:11.200
At some point it’s going to get out of control
and hurt or in Dany’s case, flame broil

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:12.460
someone.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.040
Remember the dragons only eat charred meat.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.040
Extra crispy.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:19.860
It’s followed by another new shot of Daenerys
trying to figure out how to be a real queen

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.140
now that she has all these people depending
on her.

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.330
She doesn’t want to disappoint them.

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:29.050
Quickly followed by Tyrion standing trial
in front of his father, Oberyn Martell and

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:30.050
Mace Tyrell.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:34.380
With a nice voice over that mirror’s Dany’s
sentiment of not wanting to disappoint his

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.380
father.

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:39.200
Here’s another amazing shot of Tywin sitting
on the Iron Throne.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.010
I just love the imagery here.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.920
The real power of Westeros, currently.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:47.000
Finally sitting in the visible place of highest
power.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.910
This shot of the girl with the bow confused
a lot of people, but it’s just one of Ramsay

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:54.790
Snow’s girls from back when he was tormenting
Theon with Sex.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:57.200
She looks like she joined Ramsay on a hunt.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.410
Hopefully they’re not hunting Theon again.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:04.520
Next is a new shot of Bran crawling beyond
the wall trying to reach the Three Eyed Raven.

00:04:04.520 --> 00:04:07.010
The raven is guiding Bran to him with visions.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:15.570
Then there’s another new shot of Oberyn
Martell and Ellaria Sand enjoying themselves.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:20.239
And finally a new or at least better shot
of Jon Snow killing one of his former wildling

00:04:20.239 --> 00:04:21.239
friends.

00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:26.289
For a brief second I actually thought it looked
like the same actor that played Benjen Stark

00:04:26.289 --> 00:04:28.620
in season 1, but it’s not.

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.669
So given that we’re only a few weeks away
it’s likely that they’ll release either

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:37.630
one more trailer or another long featurette
or season recap like last year.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.639
A lot of you have been asking for videos on
different characters and history videos on

00:04:41.639 --> 00:04:42.639
the great houses.

00:04:42.639 --> 00:04:47.660
But I’d like to try and do a video just
focusing on the history of dragons in the

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:48.660
world.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.690
My next Game of Thrones video will be that
Q&amp;A tomorrow.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.710
So I’ll try to get that Dragon video finished
by Friday.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:58.000
Which is Pi day, 3.14 make sure to celebrate.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:05.340
Until then click here for to watch the full
trailer again and click here for that Q&amp;A

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:06.340
video.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.050
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:08.660
High Fives!

